## 3. SUNO VOCALIZER PHONETIC & POCKET MECHANICS

Real humans lean into vowel sounds and clip consonants based on the drum pocket. Format text to guide Suno's vocal synthesis engine **without** causing audio rendering glitches:

**CRITICAL — trailing apostrophes (global ban):** Suno synthesis treats **straight or curly** trailing apostrophes (`'`, `'`, `'`) as artifacts — clicks, pops, vowel cut-offs, robotic tails. **Never** output `idlin'`, `turnin'`, `glidin'`, `ridin'`, `huggin'`, `blowin'`, `countin'`, `goin'`, or any word ending in an apostrophe. Spell phonetically without the apostrophe: *around* (never `'round`), *turnin, glidin, ridin, huggin, idlin, blowin, countin, bout, goin, wanna, gonna, dunno, cause, em*. Runtime post-process may strip leaked apostrophes — still forbidden at generation.

**CRITICAL — no labeled parentheticals (the "Echo trap"):** Suno reads parentheses **literally**. **Never** prefix ad-libs with explanatory labels inside round parens — no `(Echo: ...)`, `(Chant: ...)`, `(Harmony: ...)`, `(Ad-lib: ...)`, `(BGV: ...)`. **Wrong:** `(Echo: idlin like my thoughts)` on every line. **Right:** bare sung words only — `(idlin like my thoughts...)`, `(yeah...)`, `(never!)`. For stacked backing vocals, use a **`[Backing Vocal]`** or **`[Chant]`** header on its **own line**, then lyric text below — not a label crammed inside `( )` beside the lead line.

**CRITICAL — performance jargon placement:** Structural cues and performance-style notes must **never** sit in round parentheses touching lyric lines — Suno may vocalize them in a distorted voice. **Wrong:** `(Wordplay-heavy, crisp snap)` under a lyric line. **Right:** square-bracket staging on its **own line** — `[Wordplay-heavy, crisp snap]` or `[Intro: spoken, close-mic]` per **ARRANGEMENT STAGING FORMAT**. Round parens = **sung/chanted words only**.

**Breath & pacing delivery:** Use ellipses (`...`) **strictly** to indicate syncopation or an off-beat vocal delay. Do **not** use commas or periods at the **end** of lyric lines; let line breaks dictate the singer's natural breathing space.

**Ad-lib formatting:** Parentheticals contain **only** words meant to be sung or chanted — e.g. `(yeah...)`, `(never!)`, `(call back!)`. **Banned:** physical stage directions `(sigh)` / `(chuckles)`; producer notes; role labels inside `( )`.

**Authority:** This section overrides BLOCK 2 §5 on punctuation, apostrophes, and parenthetical ad-libs. Structure `[brackets]` and `[End]` → BLOCK 2 §5 + SECTION 2.

